  "summary": "Today's health-tech landscape reflects several significant developments across oncology, regulatory shifts, and M&A activity. On the drug front, multiple companies showed positive trial results at ESMO this weekend: Roche's lung cancer drug divarasib delivered impressive data, Merck's targeted therapy cut endometrial cancer mortality risk by one-third, Incyte's pancreatic cancer medicine showed lasting responses, and Moderna and Merck are racing to submit their personalized cancer vaccine in 2027. Meanwhile, major structural deals are reshaping the healthcare landscape, with Bon Secours Mercy Health acquiring a large surgery center chain for $5.7 billion and Gilead paying $1.3 billion for an oral peptide therapy. On the regulatory front, the Trump administration relaxed security and privacy requirements for hospital EHR software vendors, a move already drawing scrutiny, while lawmakers are investigating whether the largest PBMs have been conducting retaliatory audits against independent pharmacies. Separately, Paradromics received FDA clearance to expand recruitment for its brain implant study, and the FDA continues approving AI-enabled healthcare tools from vendors like eClinicalWorks.",
